{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When repeated tool calls receive no results, the existing loop detector fails to stop the agent during the invocation."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Unresolved repeated calls can be evicted before counting, causing the loop to go unreported even at session completion."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A missing result can prevent the detector from stopping subsequent completed calls that repeat the same result."}]}